<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply fell $700 mln in Sept 2 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $700 mln in Sept 2 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $700 million in the September 2 week to $3,759.0 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $2.4 billion to $4,753.9 billion. M-1 fell $1.5 billion to $1,098.0 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,757.9 billion versus $3,757.4 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
